WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.349
Did this animation happen in an experiment, or is it only showing how an idea could work?

q0002
00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:19.121
This episode has one job: The series uses an explicit visual grammar so an explanatory mechanism can never masquerade as an observed result.

q0003
00:00:19.121 --> 00:00:26.385
No earlier episode is required; we begin by establishing the series evidence grammar.

q0004
00:00:26.385 --> 00:00:35.212
A conceptual animation explains a relationship; a measured result reports an observation under a declared protocol.

q0005
00:00:35.212 --> 00:00:43.518
Watch for the label conceptual scene; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:43.518 --> 00:00:51.303
When we say measured result, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:51.303 --> 00:01:00.652
The term promotion status receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
00:01:00.652 --> 00:01:10.424
The next sequence uses Conceptual recognition/decomposition graph as a conceptual teaching example, not as measured benchmark evidence.

q0009
00:01:10.424 --> 00:01:15.082
Our stable example is Conceptual recognition/decomposition graph.

q0010
00:01:15.082 --> 00:01:24.854
A tiny labeled expression graph with a proposed partition, an exact witness path, a rejection/fallback path, and a promotion gate; it is never presented as a measured trace.

q0011
00:01:24.854 --> 00:01:31.597
Keep proposal, exact verification, fallback, and promotion visually stable across CRSE episodes.

q0012
00:01:31.597 --> 00:01:39.903
We now construct the Conceptual recognition/decomposition graph and name every part before interpreting it.

q0013
00:01:39.903 --> 00:01:49.675
We now render the same mechanism first as a conceptual diagram and then as a measured panel with source, scope, boundary, and uncertainty.

q0014
00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:59.447
Now introduce the persistent status badges and show how revised, negative, and not-promoted outcomes change wording without changing exactness.

q0015
00:01:59.447 --> 00:02:07.753
Now isolate conceptual, measured, revised, negative, and not-promoted scene status inside Conceptual recognition/decomposition graph.

q0016
00:02:07.753 --> 00:02:17.525
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for conceptual, measured, revised, negative, and not-promoted scene status changes.

q0017
00:02:17.525 --> 00:02:27.297
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to conceptual, measured, revised, negative, and not-promoted scene status, not to a substituted workload.

q0018
00:02:27.297 --> 00:02:33.518
Split screen: unlabeled-looking mechanism is corrected into a visibly CONCEPTUAL diagram.

q0019
00:02:33.518 --> 00:02:43.290
Teaching diagrams, proposed mechanisms, and hypotheses must be visibly labeled and may not be presented as measured traces.

q0020
00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:48.990
Read that statement only within this scope: video evidence contract.

q0021
00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:53.648
Its declared measurement boundary is editorial/visual status.

q0022
00:02:53.648 --> 00:02:57.264
The uncertainty field says not applicable.

q0023
00:02:57.264 --> 00:03:07.036
The nearest confusing lesson is Preparation, kernel, wrapper, and end-to-end time; it owns preparation, kernel, wrapper, extraction, persistence, and end-to-end timing boundaries, while this episode owns conceptual, measured, revised, negative, and not-promoted scene status.

q0024
00:03:07.036 --> 00:03:16.808
A labeled input graph enters a proposal stage whose job is to suggest a partition or route, not to certify it.

q0025
00:03:16.808 --> 00:03:25.635
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate conceptual, measured, revised, negative, and not-promoted scene status.

q0026
00:03:25.635 --> 00:03:33.420
The candidate partition remains visibly provisional until the exact verifier checks its witness conditions.

q0027
00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:43.192
An accepted path produces an exact witness; a rejected path moves to the safe fallback without changing correctness.

q0028
00:03:43.192 --> 00:03:52.964
The promotion gate is separate from exact verification because a correct result need not satisfy a performance promotion rule.

q0029
00:03:52.964 --> 00:04:00.749
Proposal, verifier, witness, rejection, fallback, and promotion keep stable shapes across every CRSE episode.

q0030
00:04:00.749 --> 00:04:09.576
A conceptual badge stays on the graph even when a later panel introduces separately sourced measurements.

q0031
00:04:09.576 --> 00:04:18.403
Changing the proposal mechanism never removes the exact verifier or the fallback path from the contract.

q0032
00:04:18.403 --> 00:04:26.188
Negative and not-promoted outcomes remain first-class states rather than disappearing from the research timeline.

q0033
00:04:26.188 --> 00:04:35.537
Task routing may select a different exact path while the admitted result and verification gate remain fixed.

q0034
00:04:35.537 --> 00:04:44.364
Every measured promotion panel names its workload, boundary, uncertainty, and source independently of this teaching graph.

q0035
00:04:44.364 --> 00:04:54.136
The starting state preserves the stable definition: A tiny labeled expression graph with a proposed partition, an exact witness path, a rejection/fallback path, and a promotion gate; it is never presented as a measured trace.

q0036
00:04:54.136 --> 00:05:03.908
After the change, the composition makes conceptual, measured, revised, negative, and not-promoted scene status inspectable: Split screen: unlabeled-looking mechanism is corrected into a visibly CONCEPTUAL diagram.

q0037
00:05:03.908 --> 00:05:12.214
A clear diagram is not evidence until its source, scope, boundary, and uncertainty are attached.

q0038
00:05:12.214 --> 00:05:19.478
Classify three matched panels as conceptual, measured, or revised before their badges appear.

q0039
00:05:19.478 --> 00:05:23.615
Read the status before reading the result.

q0040
00:05:23.615 --> 00:05:30.358
A common mistake is this: Polished motion graphics are automatically experimental evidence.

q0041
00:05:30.358 --> 00:05:39.185
Repair it by returning to the owned distinction: conceptual, measured, revised, negative, and not-promoted scene status.

q0043
00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:50.227
Use the episode's central distinction to answer: Read the status before reading the result.

q0044
00:05:50.227 --> 00:05:59.999
From here on, the badge tells you what kind of statement you are seeing before you judge the statement itself.
